 "notes": "Eot-Wash torsion-pendulum/rotating-attractor experiment (Terrano et al. 2015). Two results: (i) dipole-dipole electron spin-spin bound on (g_p^e)^2/hbar c (Fig 4, F>70 TeV) which has no canonical plane in the task table, and (ii) the monopole-dipole (CP-violating) bound on |g_p^e g_s^N|/hbar c (Fig 5, this work curve), which maps to the canonical MonopoleDipole electron-nucleon plane. Reported curve is the bold 'this work' contour extracted from the e-print vector figure sdrPRL.eps (Fig 5). x-axis m_b converted ueV->eV (x1e-6); y-axis is the dimensionless product g_s g_p (paper writes |g_p^e g_s^N|/hbar c, numerically the dimensionless coupling product in hbar=c=1). Shaded region excluded at 2 sigma (~95% CL). Flat value ~8.5e-29 matches the paper's '10^-28 level' statement; curve rises through 100 ueV and exits the top of the plot (1e-24) near 617 ueV. Here g_p is the pseudoscalar coupling of the polarized electrons and g_s the scalar coupling of the unpolarized nucleons. Limit is not dark-matter-density dependent.",
